NAME             vimrc -- Vim configuration

SYNOPSIS         vim [file ...]

DESCRIPTION      Vimrc configures Vim for files and directories.
                 File buffers edit text.
                 Directory buffers list entries.
                 Directory names end in /.
                 Plumbing resolves text in this order:
                 1. Quickfix or location jump
                 2. URL
                 3. Wiki link
                 4. Readable file:line
                 5. Readable file
                 6. Directory
                 7. Search
                 Relative plumbing uses the supplied working directory.
                 File buffers supply expand('%:h').
                 Directory buffers supply b:dir.
                 :Cmd runs in the current buffer's directory.

MOUSE            Vim sets mouse=nv.

                 Mouse button     Action
                 1                Selects text
                 1 status col 1   Grows the window, on a status line
                 double 1         Expands the bracket, quote object, or word
                 double 1 status  Closes the window, on a status line
                 C-1 status       Zooms the window, on a status line only
                 2                Runs <cWORD>
                 2 visual         Runs the selection
                 2 status         Resizes or zooms the window
                 3                Plumbs word/WORD
                 3 visual         Plumbs the selection

                 Button 2 appends stdout and stderr to +Errors.
                 Button 3 uses the plumbing order in DESCRIPTION.

DIRECTORIES      A directory buffer lists one entry per line.
                 b:dir names its directory.
                 Relative plumbing uses b:dir.
                 Global - opens the current directory.
                 <leader>B toggles the directory browser.

                 Key              Action
                 <CR>             Opens or reuses the entry
                 <leader><CR>     Plumbs the entry
                 <RightMouse>     Plumbs the entry
                 <MiddleMouse>    Runs the entry
                 <C-LeftMouse>    Runs the entry
                 -                Goes up
                 R                Reloads the directory
                 <leader>r        Renames the entry
                 <leader>d        Deletes the entry
                 <C-j>            Moves to the next window or tmux pane

COMMANDS         :Cmd [-range] [cmd]
                      Run cmd asynchronously with /bin/sh -c.
                      Send the addressed lines on stdin.
                      Append stdout and stderr to +Errors.

                 :Lint [filetype]
                      Run the linter for filetype.
                      Append the output to +Errors.

                 :Fmt [-range=%] [filetype]
                      Run the formatter for filetype.
                      Replace the addressed range or the whole buffer.

                 :Fts [args...]
                      Run the external fts command.
                      Fill the location list.

                 :Toc [pattern]
                      Fill the location list with an outline.
                      Use pattern or the default for the filetype.

                 :Sort
                      Sort the named visible windows by buffer name.

                 :B /regex/[dD]
                      List the matching buffers.
                      Delete them with d or D.

                 :Dump [file]
                      Write the session state.
                      The default file is getcwd()/vim.dump.

                 :Load [file]
                      Read the session state.
                      The default file is getcwd()/vim.dump.

                 :Send [-range] [tmux-target]
                      Send lines to a tmux pane.
                      Remember tmux-target for each window.

                 :Win
                      Open a shell in the current buffer's directory.

KEYS             The leader key is space.
                 Moving to tmux needs $TMUX and a Vim window edge.

                 Key              Action
                 <leader>!        Prompts for a shell command
                 <leader>.        Uses lcd to enter the file's directory
                 <leader>;        Sends the line to tmux
                 <leader><CR>     Plumbs the word
                 <leader><leader> Expands the selection
                 <leader>B        Toggles the directory browser
                 <leader>D        Dumps the session
                 <leader>E        Dumps the session and quits all
                 <leader>N        Edits a new file in the file's directory
                 <leader>c        Comment operator
                 <leader>cc       Comments the line
                 <leader>f        Formats the buffer
                 <leader>l        Lints the buffer
                 <leader>q        Closes the buffer
                 <leader>Q        Forces the buffer to close
                 <leader>y        Yanks the relative path through OSC 52
                 <leader>Y        Yanks the absolute path through OSC 52
                 <leader>z        Zooms the window
                 -                Opens the current directory
                 <C-j>            Moves to the next Vim window; enters tmux at the last
                 <C-k>            Moves to the previous Vim window; enters tmux at the first
                 <C-l>            Clears the search and redraws
                 <C-p>            Runs :FZF
                 +                Increases the window height

                 Visual Key       Action
                 <leader>!        Runs the selection
                 <leader>;        Sends the selection to tmux
                 <leader><CR>     Plumbs the selection
                 *                Searches for the selection

                 Go Key           Action
                 <leader>gc       GoCallers
                 <leader>gd       GoDeclsDir
                 <leader>gi       GoInfo
                 <leader>gt       GoTestFile -v

                 Terminal Key     Action
                 <C-j>            Moves to the next Vim window; enters tmux at the last
                 <C-k>            Moves to the previous Vim window; enters tmux at the first

                 Bracket          Action
                 ]a [a            Next/previous argument
                 ]b [b            Next/previous buffer
                 ]l [l            Next/previous location
                 ]q [q            Next/previous quickfix
                 ]t [t            Next/previous tab

                 Toggle           Option
                 yob              background
                 yoh              hlsearch
                 yoi              ignorecase
                 yol              list
                 yon              number
                 yop              paste
                 yor              relativenumber
                 yos              spell
                 yow              wrap

FILES            getcwd()/vim.dump
                      The default session file for :Dump and :Load

                 +Errors
                      The scratch buffer for command output

ENVIRONMENT      Vimrc needs Vim 9.1+.
                 $TMUX lets <C-j> and <C-k> move past Vim window edges.
                 OSC 52 writes yanked paths to /dev/tty.
                 Yanking paths through OSC 52 needs terminal support.
                 It also needs one of base64, openssl, or python3.
                 Vimrc does not use the Vim clipboard option.

SEE ALSO         vim(1), acme(1), plumber(4)

OWNER            callemo
